.el .ds Aq '
.TH conary 1  "conary 0.11.2" 
.SH NAME
conary \- Early\-preview Linux package manager with native\-package adoption
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconary\fR [\fB\-\-seccomp\-warn\fR] [\fB\-\-help\-advanced\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Early\-preview Linux package manager with native\-package adoption
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-seccomp\-warn\fR
Use seccomp warn mode for scriptlets instead of enforcing blocked syscalls
.TP
\fB\-\-help\-advanced\fR
List advanced packaging and platform commands
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase log verbosity (repeat for more: info, debug, trace)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Silence all logs except errors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
conary\-install(1)
Install package(s) or collection (@name)
.TP
conary\-remove(1)
Remove an installed package
.TP
conary\-update(1)
Check for and apply package updates
.TP
conary\-search(1)
Search for packages in repositories
.TP
conary\-list(1)
List installed packages
.TP
conary\-autoremove(1)
Remove orphaned packages (installed as dependencies but no longer needed)
.TP
conary\-pin(1)
Pin a package to prevent updates and removal
.TP
conary\-unpin(1)
Unpin a package to allow updates and removal
.TP
conary\-try(1)
Try a package artifact with explicit keep or rollback
.TP
conary\-system(1)
System administration (state, triggers, redirects, gc, etc.)
.TP
conary\-repo(1)
Repository management
.TP
conary\-config(1)
Configuration file management
.TP
conary\-distro(1)
Distro pinning management
.TP
conary\-self\-update(1)
Update conary itself to the latest version
.TP
conary\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Daily workflow examples:
  sudo conary install nginx \-\-dry\-run
  sudo conary install nginx \-\-yes
  sudo conary update \-\-dry\-run
  sudo conary system adopt \-\-refresh
  conary system completions bash > /tmp/conary\-completion.bash
  sudo conary system generation export \-\-path /conary/generations/1 \-\-format qcow2 \-\-output gen1.qcow2
  conaryd handles durable package jobs with the same apply\-intent boundary

Advanced packaging and platform commands: run \*(Aqconary \-\-help\-advanced\*(Aq
